-- Shipping provider area id (docs/plans/cart-checkout.md §3 "Migration 0032", D18, session 8):
-- the shipping provider changed from Komerce to Biteship (owner decision 2026-10-21), so
-- shipping_areas.komerce_destination_id becomes provider_area_id (it now holds Biteship area ids)
-- and its UNIQUE constraint is renamed to match. Owner-approved rename, 2026-10-21.
-- Generated by drizzle-kit (column rename chosen at its prompt), then read. Hand edits: this
-- header, the lock_timeout line, and RENAME CONSTRAINT in place of the generated DROP CONSTRAINT +
-- ADD CONSTRAINT UNIQUE pair (same end state and the same name in the snapshot, without dropping
-- and rebuilding the unique index, and without a moment where the column is not unique).
--
-- Backward compatibility with the previous release (session 7; CLAUDE.md expand/contract): a
-- rename instead of expand/contract is safe here only because nothing released reads or writes
-- this column. shipping_areas is empty on every environment (session 8 is the first writer), and
-- the session 7 image never queries shipping_areas at all, so rolling back to it against the
-- renamed schema behaves exactly as before. No data moves.
--
-- Locks: RENAME COLUMN and RENAME CONSTRAINT are catalog-only changes that take a brief ACCESS
-- EXCLUSIVE lock on an empty table. lock_timeout makes the migration fail fast (and roll back
-- entirely) instead of queueing behind a long-running transaction.
SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "shipping_areas" RENAME COLUMN "komerce_destination_id" TO "provider_area_id";--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "shipping_areas" RENAME CONSTRAINT "shipping_areas_komerce_destination_id_key" TO "shipping_areas_provider_area_id_key";
